E('battle of marathon|marathon', 'The Battle of Marathon was an Athenian victory over a Persian invasion.', 'It was fought in 490 BC.', 'The Athenians were outnumbered but won decisively.', 'Legend says a runner, Pheidippides, ran about 40 kilometres to Athens with the news and then died.', 'The modern marathon race is based on that legend.', 'It boosted Greek confidence against Persia.')
E('battle of salamis|salamis', 'The Battle of Salamis was a naval battle in which the Greeks defeated the Persian fleet.', 'It was fought in 480 BC.', 'The Athenian leader Themistocles lured the Persians into narrow straits.', 'The smaller Greek triremes rammed the crowded Persian ships.', 'Xerxes watched the defeat from the shore.', 'It saved Greece from Persian conquest.')
E('battle of gaugamela|gaugamela', 'The Battle of Gaugamela was Alexander the Great’s decisive victory over Persia.', 'It was fought in 331 BC, in modern Iraq.', 'Alexander faced a much larger army under Darius III.', 'He led a cavalry charge at Darius, who fled.', 'It effectively ended the Persian Empire.')
E('battle of cannae|cannae', 'The Battle of Cannae was Hannibal’s greatest victory over Rome.', 'It was fought in 216 BC in southern Italy.', 'Hannibal surrounded a much larger Roman army in a double envelopment.', 'Tens of thousands of Romans were killed in one day.', 'It is still studied in military academies.')
E('battle of actium|actium', 'The Battle of Actium was the naval battle that made Octavian master of Rome.', 'It was fought on 2 September 31 BC, off western Greece.', 'Octavian’s fleet, led by Agrippa, faced Antony and Cleopatra.', 'Cleopatra’s ships fled, and Antony followed.', 'It led to the end of the Republic and the start of the Empire.')
E('battle of tours|charles martel', 'The Battle of Tours was a Frankish victory over an Umayyad army.', 'It was fought in 732, in France.', 'Charles Martel led the Franks.', 'It halted the northward advance of Muslim forces from Spain into France.', 'Charles became known as “the Hammer”.')
E('battle of trafalgar|trafalgar|horatio nelson|nelson', 'The Battle of Trafalgar was a decisive British naval victory over France and Spain.', 'It was fought on 21 October 1805, off south-west Spain.', 'Admiral Horatio Nelson led the British fleet.', 'He signalled, “England expects that every man will do his duty.”', 'Nelson was killed by a sniper during the battle.', 'It ended Napoleon’s hopes of invading Britain.', 'Nelson’s Column in London’s Trafalgar Square honours him.')
E('battle of gettysburg|gettysburg', 'The Battle of Gettysburg was a turning point of the American Civil War.', 'It was fought from 1 to 3 July 1863, in Pennsylvania.', 'Union forces under George Meade defeated Robert E. Lee’s Confederate army.', 'Pickett’s Charge on the last day was a disastrous Confederate attack.', 'About 50,000 soldiers were killed, wounded, captured or missing.', 'Lincoln gave the Gettysburg Address there that November.')
E('battle of midway|midway', 'The Battle of Midway was a decisive US naval victory over Japan.', 'It was fought from 4 to 7 June 1942.', 'US codebreakers learned Japan’s plans in advance.', 'American aircraft sank four Japanese aircraft carriers.', 'It turned the tide of the Pacific War.')
E('battle of the bulge', 'The Battle of the Bulge was Germany’s last major offensive in the west.', 'It lasted from December 1944 to January 1945.', 'Germans attacked through the Ardennes forest in Belgium.', 'It created a “bulge” in the Allied line.', 'American troops held out at Bastogne.', 'It was the largest battle fought by the US Army in the war.')
E('dunkirk|dunkirk evacuation', 'The Dunkirk evacuation rescued Allied soldiers trapped in northern France.', 'It took place from 26 May to 4 June 1940.', 'About 338,000 British and French troops were rescued.', 'A flotilla of small civilian boats helped.', 'Churchill called it a “miracle of deliverance”.', 'It let Britain fight on.')
E('el alamein', 'The Battles of El Alamein were fought in Egypt during the Second World War.', 'The decisive second battle was in October and November 1942.', 'British forces under Montgomery defeated Rommel’s German and Italian army.', 'It ended the Axis threat to Egypt and the Suez Canal.', 'Churchill said, “Before Alamein we never had a victory. After Alamein we never had a defeat.”')
E('battle of bannockburn|bannockburn', 'The Battle of Bannockburn was a decisive Scottish victory over England.', 'It was fought on 23 and 24 June 1314.', 'Robert the Bruce led the Scots.', 'They defeated Edward II’s larger army.', 'It secured Bruce’s position as king.')
E('battle of lepanto|lepanto', 'The Battle of Lepanto was a naval battle between a Catholic alliance and the Ottoman fleet.', 'It was fought on 7 October 1571, off Greece.', 'The Holy League won decisively.', 'It was one of the last great battles of oared galleys.', 'Miguel de Cervantes was wounded there.')
E('siege of vienna', 'The Ottoman Empire besieged Vienna twice.', 'The sieges took place in 1529 and 1683.', 'Both times the city held out.', 'In 1683 a relief army led by Polish king Jan Sobieski won a decisive victory.', 'It marked the high-water mark of Ottoman expansion in Europe.')
E('battle of hastings date|stamford bridge', 'The Battle of Stamford Bridge was fought weeks before Hastings.', 'It took place on 25 September 1066.', 'King Harold II defeated a Norwegian army under Harald Hardrada.', 'Hardrada was killed.', 'It is often seen as the end of the Viking Age.')
E('battle of thermopylae date|xerxes', 'Xerxes I was the Persian king who invaded Greece.', 'He ruled from 486 to 465 BC.', 'He bridged the Hellespont with boats.', 'He won at Thermopylae but lost at Salamis.', 'He also built much of the palace at Persepolis.')
E('pearl harbor date|yamamoto', 'Isoroku Yamamoto was the Japanese admiral who planned the attack on Pearl Harbor.', 'He lived from 1884 to 1943.', 'He had studied in the United States and feared a long war with it.', 'He also planned the Midway operation.', 'The US shot down his plane in 1943.')
E('battle of austerlitz|austerlitz', 'The Battle of Austerlitz was one of Napoleon’s greatest victories.', 'It was fought on 2 December 1805.', 'It is called the Battle of the Three Emperors.', 'Napoleon defeated Russia and Austria.', 'He lured the allies into attacking his weakened right flank.')
E('battle of kursk|kursk', 'The Battle of Kursk was the largest tank battle in history.', 'It was fought in July and August 1943, in the Soviet Union.', 'Germany attacked a Soviet salient.', 'The Soviets had prepared deep defences.', 'Germany never again launched a major offensive in the east.')
E('battle of agincourt date|henry v', 'Henry V was the English king who won at Agincourt.', 'He lived from 1386 to 1422.', 'He conquered much of northern France.', 'He married Catherine of Valois, daughter of the French king.', 'He died of illness at 35.')
E('battle of yorktown|yorktown', 'The Siege of Yorktown was the last major battle of the American Revolutionary War.', 'It ended on 19 October 1781.', 'American and French forces trapped a British army under Cornwallis.', 'A French fleet blocked British escape by sea.', 'The surrender led to peace talks.')
E('battle of lexington|lexington and concord|shot heard round the world', 'The Battles of Lexington and Concord began the American Revolutionary War.', 'They were fought on 19 April 1775.', 'British troops marched to seize colonial weapons.', 'Militiamen confronted them.', 'The first shot became known as “the shot heard round the world”.')
